@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml

title Deterministic 64-column token feature hash

start
:Select exact retained text; <<#DBE4FF>>
if (non-empty?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Select semantic name; <<#A5D8FF>>
  if (present?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :Select represented operator or literal; <<#74C0FC>>
    if (present?) then (yes)
    else (no)
      :Select stable node-kind name; <<#4DABF7>>
    endif
  endif
endif
:Retain exact normalized token; <<#FFF3BF>>
:Enumerate UTF-8 byte n-grams\nfor widths 1, 2, and 3; <<#E5DBFF>>
:Hash width and bytes with fixed\n64-bit FNV-1a-style recurrence; <<#D0BFFF>>
:Choose <latex>h \bmod 64</latex> bucket and\n<latex>\pm 1</latex> from the high bit; <<#B197FC>>
:Accumulate signed counts in columns 45--108; <<#C3FAE8>>
:Return exact token plus numerical initialization; <<#63E6BE>>
stop

note right
  No vocabulary, parser, learned weight,
  random seed, or native recursion.
  Collisions are visible because the exact
  token remains beside the feature row.
end note

@enduml
